        --accent: ButtonText;
        --accent-soft: Canvas;
      }

      .hero,
      .example,
      .skip-link {
        border: 1px solid ButtonBorder;
        box-shadow: none;
      }

      .question-icon {
        border: 1px solid ButtonBorder;
      }
    }
  </style>
</head>
<body>
  <a class="skip-link" href="#main">Skip to main content</a>

  <main id="main">
    <section class="hero" aria-labelledby="faq-title">
      <p class="eyebrow">Cat FAQ</p>
      <h1 id="faq-title">Everything you were too curious to ask about cats</h1>
      <p class="intro">
        Quick answers about cat behavior, care, and the tiny mysteries that make them such iconic companions.
      </p>

      <div class="faq-list" aria-label="Cat frequently asked questions">
        <div class="example">
          <button class="question" type="button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-1" id="faq-1-button">
            Why do cats knead with their paws?
            <span class="question-icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span>
          </button>
          <div class="details" id="faq-1" role="region" aria-labelledby="faq-1-button" hidden>
            <p>Kneading is a comforting instinct that starts in kittenhood. Adult cats often do it when they feel safe, relaxed, or especially attached to you.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="example">
          <button class="question" type="button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-2" id="faq-2-button">
            Why do cats stare at me?
            <span class="question-icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span>
          </button>
          <div class="details" id="faq-2" role="region" aria-labelledby="faq-2-button" hidden>
            <p>A steady stare can mean curiosity, affection, or that your cat is waiting for something interesting to happen — like food, play, or a door to open.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="example">
          <button class="question" type="button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-3" id="faq-3-button">
            How often should I feed a cat?
            <span class="question-icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span>
          </button>
          <div class="details" id="faq-3" role="region" aria-labelledby="faq-3-button" hidden>
            <p>Most adult cats do well with two measured meals a day, but the right schedule depends on age, health, and diet. Your veterinarian can help set the best routine.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="example">
          <button class="question" type="button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-4" id="faq-4-button">
            Why do cats bring home toys or prey?
            <span class="question-icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span>
          </button>
          <div class="details" id="faq-4" role="region" aria-labelledby="faq-4-button" hidden>
            <p>This is often hunting behavior turned into a gift. Cats may be showing off a catch, practicing their skills, or including you in the game.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="example">
          <button class="question" type="button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-5" id="faq-5-button">
            How can I keep indoor cats happy?
            <span class="question-icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span>
          </button>
          <div class="details" id="faq-5" role="region" aria-labelledby="faq-5-button" hidden>
            <p>Offer daily play, vertical space, scratching posts, window views, and quiet places to rest. A predictable routine also helps many cats feel secure.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>

  <script>
    document.querySelectorAll(".example").forEach((item) => {
      const button = item.querySelector(".question");
      const panel = item.querySelector(".details");

      button.addEventListener("click", () => {
        const isOpen = button.getAttribute("aria-expanded") === "true";
        button.setAttribute("aria-expanded", String(!isOpen));
        panel.hidden = isOpen;
      });
    });
  </script>
</body>
</html>
